{{fbdoc item="title" value="__FB_ARCH__"}}----
Intrinsic define (macro string) set by the compiler

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	""__FB_ARCH__""
##
{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	Defined as a string literal containing the effective target architecture selected by the compiler, after applying options such as [[CompilerOptarch|-arch]]. The value is the compiler's canonical architecture name, not the original option text.

{{fbdoc item="ver"}}
	- Since fbc 1.20.4

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- [[CompilerOptarch|Compiler Option: -arch]]
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbx86|__FB_X86__]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbarm|__FB_ARM__]]##

{{fbdoc item="back" value="CatPgDddefines|Intrinsic Defines"}}
